    "durationMs": 272247,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Project**: Laravel 11 on PHP 8.3, scaffolded via Composer in /workspace (the existing `.git` was preserved).\n\n**Endpoints** — all verified with curl against the running server:\n- `POST /links` → `201 {\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`; URL stored and returned unchanged; custom codes honored; duplicates → `409` with `error`\n- `GET /links/{code}` → `200` / unknown → `404` JSON\n- `GET /r/{code}` → `302` with exact `Location`, atomically increments clicks exactly once (proved with 20 concurrent redirects: 2 → 22)\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- `422` JSON with `error` for malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL (scheme http/https + host required via `parse_url`/`filter_var` — Laravel's default `url` rule would wrongly accept scheme-less URLs), and invalid codes (4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`)\n\n**Key design decisions**:\n- `start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`. I confirmed in the framework source that without `--no-reload`, `artisan serve` sets non-passthrough env vars to `false` in the subprocess — which would delete DB_* and fall back to sqlite\n- Stripped all DB_* lines from `.env` so nothing can shadow the provided environment; no credentials anywhere\n- `code` column uses `utf8mb4_bin` collation — case-sensitive uniqueness and lookups, race-safe via a DB unique index plus `UniqueConstraintViolationException` handling\n- Registered routes with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`; verified the default `api` middleware group adds no throttling (would have rate-limited the test suite)\n- Added a JSON renderer for `NotFoundHttpException` so unknown paths never leak HTML\n\n**Verification**: 33 feature tests pass against MySQL; server restarted mid-test with data and click counts intact; CLI and HTTP connections confirmed to hit the same MySQL `bench` database. Server stopped, port freed, and the links table left empty for the automated suite."
